        <name>pointer</name>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput>omp::pointer</computeroutput> stores a pointer to an object allocated in memory accessible by the <computeroutput>omp</computeroutput> system. This type provides type safety when dispatching algorithms on ranges resident in <computeroutput>omp</computeroutput> memory.</para>
<para><computeroutput>omp::pointer</computeroutput> has pointer semantics: it may be dereferenced and manipulated with pointer arithmetic.</para>
<para><computeroutput>omp::pointer</computeroutput> can be created with the function <computeroutput>omp::malloc</computeroutput>, or by explicitly calling its constructor with a raw pointer.</para>
<para>The raw pointer encapsulated by a <computeroutput>omp::pointer</computeroutput> may be obtained by either its <computeroutput>get</computeroutput> member function or the <computeroutput>raw_pointer_cast</computeroutput> function.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para><computeroutput>omp::pointer</computeroutput> is not a &quot;smart&quot; pointer; it is the programmer&apos;s responsibility to deallocate memory pointed to by <computeroutput>omp::pointer</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>specifies the type of the pointee.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
