        <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput>omp::universal_pointer</computeroutput> stores a pointer to an object allocated in memory accessible by the <computeroutput>omp</computeroutput> system and host systems.</para>
<para><computeroutput>omp::universal_pointer</computeroutput> has pointer semantics: it may be dereferenced and manipulated with pointer arithmetic.</para>
<para><computeroutput>omp::universal_pointer</computeroutput> can be created with <computeroutput>omp::universal_allocator</computeroutput> or by explicitly calling its constructor with a raw pointer.</para>
<para>The raw pointer encapsulated by a <computeroutput>omp::universal_pointer</computeroutput> may be obtained by either its <computeroutput>get</computeroutput> member function or the <computeroutput>raw_pointer_cast</computeroutput> function.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para><computeroutput>omp::universal_pointer</computeroutput> is not a &quot;smart&quot; pointer; it is the programmer&apos;s responsibility to deallocate memory pointed to by <computeroutput>omp::universal_pointer</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
